> Let's keep to good advice, please.

You mean we shouldn't talk about #rubbing the lamp?

Depending on your tactics, a permanent light can be _very_ valuable -
it allows jumping, ranged use of lances and polearms and limited
casting of advanced fireball and cone of cold without needing to waste
a turn casting light every bloody single time.
I normally only rub magic lamps if i have more than one. With my track
record, my choice is often that between a disappearing djinni and a
permanent light source, and i can tell you the latter is a _lot_
better.

