> > gems
> 
> I name the hard ones 'GEM', name the soft ones 'soft' and discard them.
> Only five named or two identified gems are needed to max luck, but I
> carry a few extras in case I lose luck somehow.

Gems have the very minor benefit of giving more value per weight than
gold - which only matters if you make it out of the dungeon alive and
care about score.

There are some ways of telling glass and real gems apart: unicorns
will "not care about your junk" or somesuch if you toss them a
non-individually named (or properly identified) piece of glass; glass
golems are _made_ of glass and will typically leave several pieces of
glass upon destruction.

